      "description": "One line of a log. `at` is null on a line that carries no timestamp prefix, and `line` is then the whole line. `command` is an additive convenience: the agent writes the verb into its own log prefix, and splitting it once here saves every client the same regular expression.",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "at": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/isoOrNull"
        },
        "line": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "command": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/textOrNull"
